WEBVTT

00:20:55.454 --> 00:21:01.329
and which ones seem to be idiosyncratic
to either individuals or to groups

00:21:01.329 --> 00:21:02.329
or cultures?

00:21:03.079 --> 00:21:11.079
Well. You know, the facial expression
that goes with bigging, pouting,

00:21:11.079 --> 00:21:14.538
the lips, the facial expression
that goes with fear,

00:21:14.538 --> 00:21:18.496
drawing the lips right back and
having the mouth wide open,

00:21:19.038 --> 00:21:22.829
the facial expression that
shows laughter and play,

00:21:23.663 --> 00:21:28.996
I think we find them in chimps of all
different groups that have been studied

00:21:28.996 --> 00:21:32.288
and in captive chimps as well,
for the most part.